# File: module/Application/view/layout/layout.phtml, line: 1203
msgid "Weddings"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 254
msgid "Plan your dream wedding in the stunning landscapes of Peru, from beach ceremonies to mountain vows."
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 265
msgid "More"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 266
msgid "Savor the flavors of Peru's world-renowned cuisine, shop at local markets, and relax in top-notch spas."
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 293
msgid "Upcoming Attractions"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 295
msgid "Located on top of a mountain in the middle of a tropical forest, it is considered the tourist attraction par excellence in Peru. The historic sanctuary is a place that captivates tourists not only for its dazzling architectural beauty, but also for its important historical-cultural legacy, which has led it to be recognized and admired throughout the world."
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 523
msgid "Mystical Machu Picchu"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 524
msgid "Discover the ancient Inca city of Machu Picchu, a UNESCO World Heritage site and one of the New Seven Wonders of the World. Immerse yourself in its historical grandeur and the breathtaking views of the Andean mountains"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 532
msgid "Culinary Delights"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 533
msgid "Indulge in Peru's world-renowned cuisine, a tantalizing fusion of flavors that has earned global acclaim. From fresh ceviche to hearty quinoa dishes, each bite is a testament to the country's rich culinary heritage"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 541
msgid "Diverse Landscapes"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 542
msgid "Experience Peru's geographic diversity, from the arid plains of the coast to the lush Amazon rainforest. This land of contrasts offers an array of natural wonders and outdoor adventures for every type of traveler"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 550
msgid "Cultural Richness"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 551
msgid "Engage with Peru's vibrant culture and traditions. Witness colorful festivals, explore pre-Columbian ruins, and learn about the legacy of ancient civilizations that continue to influence modern Peruvian society"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 562
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 569
msgid "The Lost City of the Incas"
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 563
msgid "Nestled high in the Andes, Machu Picchu stands as a testament to the Inca Empire's architectural prowess and mystical allure. Constructed in the mid-15th century, this royal estate was both a retreat for Inca emperors and a site for religious ceremonies."
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 564
msgid "The city's strategic location, between the peaks of Machu Picchu and Huayna Picchu, provided a formidable natural defense, and its design reflects a harmonious blend with its mountainous surroundings. Despite its grandeur, Machu Picchu was abandoned shortly after the Spanish conquest, its existence becoming a local secret for centuries."
msgstr ""
#
# File: module/Application/view/application/destinations/peru.phtml, line: 565
msgid "The \"Lost City\" was brought to global attention by Hiram Bingham, who, guided by local residents, rediscovered the ruins in 1911. Since then, it has become an icon of Inca civilization and a symbol of Peru."
msgstr ""
